VeridianOS: find Boost through its own CMake package

src/CMakeLists.txt asks for Boost in MODULE mode, through CMake's
FindBoost, which CMake 3.30 deprecated and CMake 4 removes under policy
CMP0167 (set to NEW for the whole stack, tools/cross/cmake/
kde-defaults.cmake). Boost has shipped its own CMake package
(BoostConfig.cmake) since 1.70, and the sysroot's Boost is installed with
it; the search is now in CONFIG mode. The package sets Boost_INCLUDE_DIRS,
which the code uses, as FindBoost did.

--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 
 # Boosting us a bit
 
-find_package(Boost ${Boost_MINIMUM_VERSION} MODULE REQUIRED)
+find_package(Boost ${Boost_MINIMUM_VERSION} CONFIG REQUIRED)
 set_package_properties(Boost PROPERTIES
     DESCRIPTION "Boost C++ Libraries"
     URL "https://www.boost.org"
